        Settings, Appearance. design-v3.md 10.11 and 16.1.

        A label and a caption for a switch, which is fixed interface copy and not an
        observation, so it belongs here. The caption says what the setting does and
        nothing about the person who turns it on: design-v3.md 16.4 forbids the app
        announcing calm mode anywhere else, and that rule starts with this string.

        The row itself lands with the Settings screen in phase 11, issue #10. These are
        the words it uses, fixed here in phase 3b alongside the setting they name.
    -->
